          'In major processing centers such as Hojai in Assam and Chanthaburi in Thailand, agarwood sorting generates multiple physical grades. As artisans work with small curved chisels to clean non-resinated white wood from valuable core pieces, fine shards and dislodged resin nodules fall into collection troughs below the workbenches.',
          'This material is carefully sieved through brass mesh screens to separate fine dust from coarse granules. The coarse fraction, rich in dense heartwood particles, is designated as premium Digga.',
